pokebw2-blackfixes.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): five places where Black's port already
had a 64-bit fix in the same code (src/, lib/) and Black 2's copy still had the DS number or a 32-bit cast.
field_ground_anime.c's FIELD_TERRAIN_SRT_ANMOBJ_SIZE: each map chunk's SRT animation object is a fixed 0x80 block, the
NNSG3dAnmObj record (0x1c on the DS, 0x30 here: four pointers) and its material map after it, room for 50 materials on
the DS and 43 here; a chunk model with more wrote its map over the next block's heap header in the field heap (Black 2's
Opelucid east plaza, after the trainer at 492,173: SIGSEGV in InsertMBlock at the next map unload). Now
WORK_AREA_SIZE(0x80), as Black's src/ov021/field_ground_anime.c. plist_demo.c: the party list's form change particles'
work, 0x5000, WORK_AREA_SIZE as Black's (the SPL manager's emitters hold pointers). scrcmd_network.c: a 4-byte block that
holds a pointer, sizeof(u16 *). union_oneself.c: the trainer card copy, sizeof(TrainerCardData) (0x680 here), not 0x678.
mystery_gift_data.h: the gift Pokemon's names passed to PokeParty_SetParam as uintptr_t, not u32 (a truncated pointer).
Found with pokebw2-heapreport.patch's BWPORT_HEAPLOG=2 and a scan of Black's 64-bit commits for each removed literal or
(u32) cast still in pokebw2.

